meta {
  name: Submit Application (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/{{admissionCycleId}}/application/submit
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Final submit. Does NOT decrement any seats — like a real college
  admission, submitting is only a request; a seat is never consumed just
  by applying. Seat decrement happens later, when a college admin approves
  the application (that admin-side action doesn't exist yet — this is
  intentional, not an oversight).

  Requires: application still in "draft" status, primary course's fee paid
  (feePaymentStatus === "paid" — see the payments endpoints), declaration
  accepted, and at least one active course selection. Runs atomically
  inside a single DB transaction: each ApplicationCourse.status ->
  "submitted" with a status log entry, then Application.formStatus ->
  "submitted" and submittedAt is set.
}
